{"type":"message","id":"76c20645","parentId":"28abe435","timestamp":"2026-05-18T15:56:17.714Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I can see the feishu channel config. The current `groupPolicy` is `\"open\"` which means it allows all groups by default. But the error says \"group oc_76f7651cb976ad84d66158beb2f29be2 not in groupAllowFrom (groupPolicy=allowlist)\". \n\nWait, but the config shows `\"groupPolicy\": \"open\"`. That's odd. Maybe the actual running config is different from what's in the file, or maybe the `groupPolicy` was changed since the last restart.\n\nActually wait - looking at the error message more carefully: `(groupPolicy=allowlist)` - but the config shows `groupPolicy: \"open\"`. This mismatch suggests either:\n\n\n1. The running config has a different value\n2. The error is coming from a specific account's config\n\nThe error message shows `feishu[main]` which means account `main`. Let me check if there's an account-level override that I missed, since the `main` account might have its own `groupPolicy` setting that differs from the channel-level config.\n\nLooking at the account config structure, each account (`main`, `lucus`, etc.) only has `appId`, `appSecret`, `name`, and `domain` - no `groupPolicy` override there either. But wait, the config actually shows `\"groupPolicy\": \"open\"` at the top channel level, so it should be allowing all groups. Yet the error says the group isn't in `groupAllowFrom` with `groupPolicy=allowlist`. This suggests either the running config differs from what's in the file, or I need to restart for changes to take effect. Let me query the actual running config instead of just reading the file.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-7b562050-143e-48b0-a763-7bd2ad3ba38f","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"openclaw config show channels.feishu 2>&1"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxa