{"type":"message","id":"17a02c23","parentId":"f03c4fa3","timestamp":"2026-05-19T03:49:53.648Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to:\n1. Create a Feishu document titled \"文档编辑测试\"\n2. Transfer ownership to them\n\nI need to use the feishu_doc tool to create the document. The owner should be the sender's open_id from the metadata: `ou_f786171f9e21bf5a09c3116b2e77aaff`\n\nBut wait - I don't have a direct `feishu_doc` tool available in my tool list. Let me check the skills available... I read the feishu-doc SKILL.md earlier. The tool is `feishu_doc` with actions like `create`.\n\nI don't see `feishu_doc` in my available tools though. \n\nI'm looking at my available tools and I don't have `feishu_doc` directly - I have `read`, `write`, `edit` for file operations and `exec`, but not the Feishu document tool. The skill mentions it's activated when the user mentions Feishu docs, but that doesn't automatically give me access to the tool itself. Let me check if there's a command or exec-based approach to interact with Feishu instead. I'm realizing I don't have direct access to the `feishu_doc` tool despite the SKILL.md documentation describing it as available. The tool documentation shows it should handle document creation with an `action: \"create\"` parameter taking a title and owner_open_id, but I'm not seeing it in my actual available tools list. I need to figure out if this is something I can invoke through a different mechanism or if there's another approach to creating the document. Looking at my available tools, I don't have feishu_doc listed, so I can't directly create the document even though the skill documentation describes how to use it. The tool availability should be filtered by policy according to the system prompt, but I'm not seeing feishu_doc in my actual tool list. I should let the user know I don't have access to this functionality, though I could potentially explore alternative approaches if they exist. I'm re-reading the system prompt more carefully now. The tool descriptions are guidance for how to use external tools, not guarantees they'll be available. Tools are filtered by policy, and I should only use what's actually available in the `functions` namespace. Since `feishu_doc` isn't listed there, I need to be honest with the user that I don't have access to this tool, rather than assuming I can somehow invoke it or work around it. I don't have access to the feishu_doc tool, so I can't create the document directly—I'll need to let the user know this limitation.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n我没有 `feishu_doc` 工具的调用权限，无法直接操作飞书文档。这应该是 OpenClaw 技能层面的能力，但我这边的 tool list 里没有暴露出来。\n\n需要你先确认一下 OpenClaw 这边 feishu doc 工具是否已经启用：\n\n```bash\nopenclaw config show channels.feishu.tools\n```\n\n如果显示 `doc: true` 就说明已启用。如果没有，可以执行：\n\n```bash\nopenclaw config set channels.feishu.tools.doc true\n```\n\n然后重启 gateway，再让我操作。或者你也可以在飞书里直接手动创建好文档，然后把文档链接发给我，我来测试写入和权限转让。"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":33678,"output":669,"cacheRead":208,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":34555,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1779162571963,"responseId":"chatcmpl-f44abb4a-da85-4221-8b7b-9cad86274e15"}}
